  "result": "Perfect! All 170 tests pass. I've added payment terms support to invoices:\n\n**Payment Terms in `createInvoice`:**\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `terms` \u2014 optional, defaults to `'NET30'`\n- Valid values: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'`, `'EOM'`\n- Invalid terms return `TERMS_INVALID` error\n\n**Sets on invoice:**\n- `invoice.terms` \u2014 the payment terms selected\n- `invoice.dueDate` \u2014 calculated based on terms (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n\n**Term calculations (all in UTC):**\n\n**`NET14`** \u2014 Due 14 days after issue date\n- Issue: 2026-10-07 \u2192 Due: 2026-10-21\n\n**`NET30`** \u2014 Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n- Issue: 2026-10-07 \u2192 Due: 2026-11-06\n\n**`EOM`** \u2014 Due on the last day of the issue date's month\n- Issue: 2026-10-07 \u2192 Due: 2026-10-31\n- Issue: 2024-02-15 (leap year) \u2192 Due: 2024-02-29\n- Issue: 2026-02-15 (non-leap) \u2192 Due: 2026-02-28\n- Issue: 2026-12-15 \u2192 Due: 2026-12-31\n\n**Example:**\n```javascript\nconst inv1 = createInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DEV-HOUR', qty: 100 }],\n  // defaults to NET30\n}).value;\n// { issueDate: '2026-10-07', terms: 'NET30', dueDate: '2026-11-06', ... }\n\nconst inv2 = createInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DEV-HOUR', qty: 100 }],\n  terms: 'NET14'\n}).value;\n// { issueDate: '2026-10-07', terms: 'NET14', dueDate: '2026-10-21', ... }\n```\n\n**Test coverage:** 11 new tests covering:\n- Default NET30 terms\n- NET14, NET30, EOM calculations\n- Leap years and month boundaries\n- Year boundaries\n- Invalid terms\n- Integration with discounts\n\nAll 170 tests pass \u2713",
